  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at the Knitting Factory in New York on March 3, 2004, delivering an eighteen-song set that lasted approximately sixty-five minutes [1]. This audience recording, captured on a Sony Mini Disc recorder with Radio Shack microphones, is the only archived performance of this specific show [1]. The setlist features a mix of acoustic and full-band arrangements, including the rare track \"Going to Queens\" and the legendary \"rules for the set,\" which is the only archived performance of that song [1]. Listeners reviewing this specific recording note that the sound quality is generally praised, with one user awarding five stars for the audio despite a lower overall rating [2]. Another listener highlights John’s songwriting and the band’s presence on the archive, describing the show as good with solid sound [3]. A third reviewer observes that the newer songs in semi-stripped down guitar and bass versions are enjoyable, and the performance intensifies when drums are added [4]. While one user found the recording difficult to listen to in parts [6], another called it a great set with great quality [5]. This show is the fifty-sixth in the archive’s collection for the performer, following a March 2, 2004, date at The First Unitarian Church [7].",
